  "X_ITE 16.6.0 draws 400 view-aligned slices with no opacity correction; the bridge marches a ray on the same planes but accumulates in float where X_ITE blends 8 bit per slice, so a volume of faint alpha differs by tens of levels (the tests check saturated colours)",
  "bboxSize and bboxCenter are kept and change nothing (they only matter for culling, as in X_ITE)",
  "opaque shapes that cut through a volume are not cut per pixel (the box is depth tested as a whole)",
  "fog and clip planes are not applied to the volume"
